# .claudeignore — files Claude must never read, write, edit, grep or cat.
#
# ENFORCEMENT LIVES IN .claude/settings.json (permissions.deny). That file is
# what Claude Code actually reads; this one is the human-readable index of the
# same list, in gitignore syntax, so the intent is visible at the repo root and
# other tools (ripgrep honours .ignore-style files) can reuse it.
#
# If you add a pattern here, add the matching Read/Write/Edit/Bash triples to
# .claude/settings.json too, or it will not be enforced.

# ── database connections: holds host, user and PASSWORD per tenant ───────────
db_config.py
**/db_config.py

# ── environment files: SAS tokens, storage accounts, output paths ────────────
.env
.env.*
*.env
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
env.example
**/env.example
d2s.env
**/d2s.env

# ── keys and credentials ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.credentials.json
**/.credentials.json
*.pem
*.key
**/*.pem
**/*.key
id_rsa*
**/id_rsa*
.netrc
**/.netrc

# ── notes ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# db_config.example.py and env.example templates in source_doc_viewer are the
# blank skeletons — they are meant to be readable, but the .env* patterns above
# catch env.example anyway. Fill in the real values only in db_config.py and a
# .env, both of which are gitignored and denied above.
